     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Do you know much at all about ggplot and the shape of data, particularly a data frame, that is needed? If not, I would starting getting familiar with ggplot and what it has available. Hadley Wickham&#39;s ggplot2 book and Winston Chang&#39;s R Graphics Cookbook are great resources. If you have a specific question after looking into things, then this mailing list can help with specific questions.<div><br></div><div>If you are stuck on the data manipulation, R has the plyr and reshape2 packages that are quite helpful, so I would read up on those. And, yes, Stack Exchange would likely be a better resource for questions here than this mailing list. </div><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br><div></div></div></div></div>"
